        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Parodia, Thalictrum, Parodia arnostiana\n- Plant families: Cactaceae, Ranunculaceae\n- Places: Argentina, Peru, Bolivia, Brazil, Colombia, Uruguay, temperate regions\n\nFacts:\n- Parodia is a genus of flowering plants in the cactus family Cactaceae.\n- Parodia is native to the uplands of Argentina, Peru, Bolivia, Brazil, Colombia, and Uruguay.\n- Thalictrum is a genus of 120 to 200 species of herbaceous perennial flowering plants in the Ranunculaceae family.\n- Thalictrum is native mostly to temperate regions.\n- Parodia arnostiana is a species of cactus in the genus Parodia.",
